{
    // SDD-L11-T9/T10. Config files the root tsconfig cannot see, checked with the same options.
    //
    // Two separate blind spots. First: the root `include` only matches `**/*.ts(x)`, so `allowJs` is inert and
    // no `.js` file is in the compiler's scope — a `// @ts-check` header there would show squiggles
    // in an editor and prove nothing in CI. This project adds the checkable ones to the same
    // compiler options without touching the root config, and `npm run typecheck` runs both.
    //
    // Only `jest.config.js` is listed. The other three jest files use bare `jest`, `beforeEach` and
    // friends, which have no ambient declarations here: `@types/jest` is not installed (jest@29 ships
    // `@jest/globals` for explicit imports instead). Enabling `@ts-check` on them today produces 25
    // errors that are all "this global has no type", not real defects, so they stay unchecked until
    // either `@types/jest` is added or the mocks import from `@jest/globals`.
    "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
    "compilerOptions": {
        // The root config is incremental; a second project must not fight it for the same buildinfo.
        "incremental": false
    },
    // Second: TypeScript's include globs skip directories whose name starts with a dot, so
    // `**/*.ts` never matched `.storybook/`. Migrating those files to TypeScript in T7 therefore
    // typechecked nothing until they were named here — found by injecting a deliberate error and
    // watching `npm run typecheck` stay green.
    // Third blind spot, found while adding the visual suite: the root config excludes `e2e/**/*`
    // and `playwright.config.ts` outright, so the whole end-to-end layer was never typechecked.
    // The visual suite is several hundred lines of TypeScript whose job is to be trusted, so it is
    // checked here with the same options as the app.
    //
    // This listed only `e2e/visual/**` at first, because widening it surfaced four pre-existing
    // `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` errors in `fixtures.ts`, `routes.test.ts` and
    // `scroll-surfaces.test.ts` — unrelated to the visual suite, and not worth holding its baseline
    // hostage to. That follow-up change has now landed, with real guards rather than assertions, so
    // the glob covers the whole directory and no Playwright file is unchecked.
    //
    // Note this project's `exclude` replaces the root's rather than extending it, which is what
    // brings `*.test.ts` into scope here: the root config excludes them everywhere.
    "include": [
        "jest.config.js",
        ".storybook/**/*.ts",
        ".storybook/**/*.tsx",
        "playwright.config.ts",
        "e2e/**/*.ts"
    ],
    "exclude": ["node_modules"]
}
